  "description": "ASP.NET host for a meta framework front end — Nuxt, TanStack Start, SolidStart, SvelteKit, Analog or Next.js — running beside your C# in ONE container. Kestrel owns the public port and answers /_rask itself; the framework's own Node server is a supervised child on loopback, and everything else is forwarded to it with WebSocket upgrade and unbuffered streaming intact. Pairs with Rask.Cqrs.Server, which gives server-side rendering a typed wire back into your C#. Distinct from Rask.Spa.Hosting, which serves a static bundle and needs no Node at runtime.",
